# .tiercheckignore — hyphenated backticked tokens that tier-check's PROSE-REF class
# reaches, and which are NOT component references. Same format and same hard rule as
# .linkcheckignore: `file_glob -> token_glob # reason`, and a rule with no `# reason`
# is a hard error. Suppressed counts print on every run, including a clean one, so this
# debt cannot go quiet.
#
# Read the PROSE-REF section of boot-kit/scripts/tier-check.py before adding a line.
# The class was measured, not guessed — on the tree that carried the defect it narrowed
# 873 backticked tokens to 10, and 4 of those 10 were the defect. Suppressing a finding
# because it is inconvenient re-opens exactly the gap this class closes. Every rule here
# says why the token is not a component; none says "not a defect".

skills/agent-notepad/*.md -> proj-* # example notepad directory names in agent-notepad's own docs (`proj-arbbot`, `proj-bugs`), not components
*.md -> platform-libs # a memory CATEGORY, paired with `patterns` in the same clause — where a lesson is filed, not a thing that is invoked
skills/df-context-store/substrate-template/CLAUDE-stanza.md -> pre-commit # the git hook of that name, installed by the substrate; not a skill or agent
